A||||6||REDHOTT88||My 88 just pulled a hissy fit then stopped!!! WTF!!||||1||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||12-06-2001||07:58 PM||||O.K. It's 67 degrees up here today. Decided to go for a little ride... started up my 88 Formula V6, let it run about 3 minutes, then took off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Drove about 1/2 mi. came to stop sign, stopped, then proceeded.... all of a sudden she started sputtering, gasping, almost dying out(something like wet wires, but really worse!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I downshifted, if I kept full throttle in 2nd, it subsided a little. Shift up to third it coughs and gags.<P>I pulled over to a gas station, shut it off and bought a newspaper, thinking the worst and that the car would have to sit there all night.<P>I started it for shits and grins, and it seemed o.k. I drove off and it's fine...<P>What was that all about?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||12-06-2001||08:15 PM||||You might have gotten some water in the fuel on the last fill up. When is the last time you put a bottle of dry gas in it???||||reg||1
Z||000002||WampusCat||12-06-2001||08:17 PM||||You obviously had a troll or a small wood nymph interfering with the 'harmony' of your engine.  When you stopped at the station, it probably jumped out of the car to go inside and look for a twinkie.  Good move.||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-06-2001||08:19 PM||||Ummmm. dry gas?<P>Actually, I just got the car in August.. haven't put any in. But, when I stopped at the gas station, I did fill it up with premium before restarting. It was on 1/4 b4.<P>That was a troll? Uh Oh.. I hope I don't get arrested, I thought it was a mouse running from my engine and shot it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-06-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000004||California Kid||12-06-2001||08:37 PM||||Hey Redhot.....Best to put some (dry gas) in there, it's the only thing that will remove any condensate water from your fuel tank. A side benefit is that it will also keep your tank from rusting out from the inside. You should put a can in about every 6 months, my opinion (too many stations don't pump the condensate off like they should, even heard that some stations, when low on gas, add some water to it).||||reg||1
Z||000005||REDHOTT88||12-06-2001||08:48 PM||||Really? I didn't think it would do that much...<P>But I'll take your word on it!!!<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Two88GTs||12-06-2001||10:59 PM||||Your gas gauge read 1/4 full?  How much gas did you put in?  A LOT of Fieros have gas gauges that are notoriously inaccurate, i.e. 1/4 full really means running close to empty.||||reg||1
